From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 14:44:49 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 174/207] server: deadline_s ends a reply at its deadline with
 every token, usage and receipt

A request may name "deadline_s" (seconds, more than 0, at most 1000000). At that time the server cancels the
engine itself, still commits the tokens the engine gives before its finished event, and labels the reply
finish_reason "deadline". The final response keeps usage, token_ids/token_sha256 and the runner receipt, so a
deadline-cut reply carries native token telemetry (W9-SPEC item 1). Without the field nothing changes.

test-request-deadline-host: a forced deadline (finish deadline, the late token kept, ids and receipt), the field
off against a deadline the reply never meets (reply, token sha and every stream delta the same), bad values
refused.

(cherry picked from commit dadaa0e2400c616f80fe3fe0b8b57f812fd55f7f)
